<title>BELGIUM: EU sets new changes veal early marketing premia.</title>
<headline>EU sets new changes veal early marketing premia.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's beef management committee revised the early marketing premia for veal on Friday, an Commision official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The changes followed a complaint by France at this week's farm council that the system introduced because of the mad cow crisis was favouring Dutch producers and distorting their market,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The French complained that producers in the Netherlands were gaining a market advantage because their animals were heavier than those of French producers.</p>
<p>The revised premia rate per animal were given as:</p>
<p>Period April 14 to June 30 (1997):</p>
<p>Up to 110 kg increased to 80 ecus from 70 ecus</p>
<p>Between 110-120 kg unchanged at 65 ecus</p>
<p>More than 120 kg reduced to 50 ecus from 60 ecus</p>
<p>From July 1 (1997)</p>
<p>Up to 110 kg unchanged at 65 ecus</p>
<p>Between 110-120 kg reduced to 57.5 ecus from 62.5</p>
<p>More than 120 kg reduced to 50 ecus from 60 ecus.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
